# Google OAuth2 Integration & Deployment Architecture

To make connecting to email as simple as possible (and avoid App Passwords entirely), we will implement a "Sign in with Google" (OAuth2) flow for the Email section. 

Since you mentioned you want to host this on **GitHub Pages** for your AI business (Sentiq Labs), there is an important architectural requirement to understand: **GitHub Pages can only host static websites (HTML/CSS/JS)**. It cannot run the Python/FastAPI backend, connect to databases (SQLite), or run the AI agent loop.

## The Architecture for Sentiq Labs
To achieve your goal of hosting the UI on GitHub pages while keeping the agent functional for everything:
1. **Frontend (GitHub Pages):** We will eventually configure the React app to build statically and deploy to your GitHub Pages URL (e.g., `sentiqlabs.github.io`).
2. **Backend (PaaS):** The Python backend (which runs the AI Agent, connects to IMAP, and stores data) will need to be deployed to a backend hosting provider like Render, Railway, or Heroku. The GitHub Pages frontend will be configured to talk to this backend via API calls.

## Proposed Changes (OAuth2 Implementation)

We will implement the OAuth2 flow so users can securely connect their Gmail without an App Password.

### 1. Backend (`core/models.py` & `routes/email.py`)
- **[MODIFY] `core/models.py`**: Update the `EmailAccount` table to store `access_token`, `refresh_token`, and `token_expires_at` instead of an `encrypted_password`.
- **[MODIFY] `routes/email.py`**: Add `/email/auth/google/login` and `/email/auth/google/callback` endpoints to handle the OAuth2 redirect flow.
- **[MODIFY] `core/integrations/email_client.py`**: Update `fetch_inbox` and `send_email` to use the `XOAUTH2` authentication mechanism instead of basic password authentication.

### 2. Frontend (`EmailManager.jsx`)
- **[MODIFY] `EmailManager.jsx`**: Replace the manual IMAP/SMTP App Password form with a "Sign in with Google" button. When clicked, this will redirect the user through the Google OAuth consent screen.

## User Review Required

> [!WARNING]
> **Google Cloud Setup Required**
> To make "Sign in with Google" work, you (as the developer of Sentiq Labs) will need to go to the [Google Cloud Console](https://console.cloud.google.com/), create a project, configure the OAuth Consent Screen, and generate a **Client ID** and **Client Secret**. 
> You will then need to put these credentials into a `.env` file on your backend server. The app cannot do this automatically.

